# S5720S-28TP-PWR-LI-ACL / V200R019C10SPC500, 2026-10-14
# Production-scope template, NOT yet deployed as /64.
# Both /128 WAN paths and both cross-group router ping/TCP22 paths were tested.
# This hardware rejects IPv6 destination matching in VLAN/GE0/0/4 inbound policies.
# Therefore use one SOURCE-ONLY policy on each VLAN, with edge LAN hairpin forwarding.
# Prerequisite: deploy the matching ipv6-pbr-hairpin-a/b.nft.example at each edge first.
# Core/edges must have specific internal routes; never point edge WAN defaults at core.
# Keep these policies OFF VLAN3/4: edge-returned traffic must follow the core route table.
# No match-order, precedence, physical-port binding, or LOCAL permit behavior is used.
# Current source prefixes are PD snapshots; update after an actual PD prefix change.
# User confirmed empty applied-record after testing; check bindings again before applying.
# ACL3981/3982 were created for this task. Check no unrelated rules before replacing rule5.
# Existing VLANIF addresses, PD clients, OSPFv3 and security ACLs stay in their own config.

system-view
acl ipv6 3981
 undo rule 5
 rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7866:a785:: 64
 quit
acl ipv6 3982
 undo rule 5
 rule 5 permit ipv6 source 2408:8207:7865:78b1:: 64
 quit
traffic classifier PBR6_A_SOURCE operator or
 if-match ipv6 acl 3981
 quit
traffic classifier PBR6_B_SOURCE operator or
 if-match ipv6 acl 3982
 quit
traffic behavior PBR6_TO_A
 redirect ipv6-nexthop link-local FE80::B83B:17FF:FE74:32D0 interface Vlanif 3
 statistics enable
 quit
traffic behavior PBR6_TO_B
 redirect ipv6-nexthop link-local FE80::5434:4EFF:FEFA:68A4 interface Vlanif 4
 statistics enable
 quit
traffic policy PBR6_A_EGRESS
 classifier PBR6_A_SOURCE behavior PBR6_TO_A
 quit
traffic policy PBR6_B_EGRESS
 classifier PBR6_B_SOURCE behavior PBR6_TO_B
 quit
vlan 1
 traffic-policy PBR6_A_EGRESS inbound
 quit
vlan 2
 traffic-policy PBR6_B_EGRESS inbound
 quit
return
display traffic-policy applied-record

# Enable VLAN1 client RA only AFTER both edge fragments and both /64 policies are active.
# Confirm Vlanif1 still has its current ng3prefix /64 and valid PIO/autonomous flag.
# Normal clients use the core's link-local address as IPv6 default gateway.
# system-view
# interface Vlanif 1
#  undo ipv6 nd ra halt
#  quit
# return
# Validate real clients in VLAN1/2: correct source prefix, WAN path, authorized internal
# TCP/UDP, same-VLAN ND, RA, OSPFv3, MTU/ICMPv6 and policy counters, then save.
# save

# ROLLBACK core bindings (does not delete objects or change IPv4):
# system-view
# vlan 1
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_A_EGRESS inbound
#  quit
# vlan 2
#  undo traffic-policy PBR6_B_EGRESS inbound
#  quit
# return
# If VLAN1 RA was newly enabled here, restore its original halted state on rollback.
# Edge rollback removes only this fragment's two rules by recorded handles,
# then its two named sets; remove its persistent include as well.
